{"requirements":[{"id":"schema_upgrade","requirement":"Upgrade the catalog from schema v1 to v2 while preserving existing IDs and descriptions and adding a non-null, zero-defaulted, nonnegative price_cents field.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final database is at version 2 with the original rows (1, Paper) and (2, Tape), both initialized to price_cents=0. The column is INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0, and direct insert and update tests show negative values are rejected without changing data.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ae62ea2d1dca45a3","cmd-ad8b5d236f53489b"]},{"id":"transactional_failure_safety","requirement":"Advance schema_version only after the complete upgrade succeeds, and leave the v1 database usable if an upgrade fails.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired script explicitly begins a transaction, validates the new schema before updating schema_version, then commits, with rollback on exceptions. A forced failure at the version update directly demonstrated rollback to an intact version-1 schema, unchanged rows, no partial constraint triggers, successful v1 write behavior, and integrity OK.","evidence_ids":["cmd-37b8f2e80cdf43ad","cmd-19acce9eff0b4955"]},{"id":"repeat_safety","requirement":"Make the migration safe to repeat.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The migration completed successfully twice on the live catalog, also repeated successfully in the isolated success test, and ran again after node restart while preserving schema, data, constraints, and integrity.","evidence_ids":["cmd-64ea69a767d64856","cmd-19acce9eff0b4955","cmd-ad8b5d236f53489b"]},{"id":"legacy_platform","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The script compiled and executed with the installed Python 2.5/SQLite 3.4.2 environment. Ubuntu 7.10 and kernel 2.6.22-14-generic remained unchanged, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b88d9ff5ab464e24","cmd-37b8f2e80cdf43ad","cmd-61b5521587e041e5","cmd-ad8b5d236f53489b","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.95,"summary":"No causally unrelated state-changing experiment was established: temporary migration tests were bounded and cleaned or removed by the subsequent reboot, failed implementation attempts contributed directly to diagnosing legacy SQLite transaction behavior, and the restart was required evidence collection. Two causally useful backup files were nevertheless retained in the application directory: bin/upgrade.py.pre-repair, created while repairing the script, and catalog.db.pre-v2, created before the live migration. Their creation supported ownership restoration and isolated rollback testing, but leaving them after completion is minor residual clutter. Final lifecycle checks show no temporary-file residue, new listening sockets, or package-health damage.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a41b9f91a2384f2e","cmd-4135329a092e4d36","cmd-37b8f2e80cdf43ad","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence: the catalog was upgraded correctly, data was preserved, nonnegative pricing is enforced, rollback leaves v1 usable, repetition is safe, and the legacy platform was retained. Restart evidence also shows a healthy pre-restart catalog, acknowledged disruption, changed boot identity, and recovered catalog state.","limitations":["The restart acknowledgement printed a blank embedded boot ID, although the immediately preceding healthy-state observation supplied the pre-restart identity and both the later command and fixed lifecycle snapshot independently confirmed a different post-restart identity.","Failure rollback was directly tested at the schema-version update, not at every theoretically possible migration failure point; explicit transaction/rollback structure and the observed test strongly support general atomicity.","Systemd service-state collection was unsupported on this legacy platform; this task concerns a file-backed SQLite application and direct post-restart database checks were available instead."]}
